# Line endings are load-bearing here: this project ships shell scripts.
#
# git's Windows default is core.autocrlf=true, which converts text files to CRLF on
# checkout. bash treats the carriage return as part of the shebang and refuses the file
# with "/usr/bin/env bash^M: bad interpreter" - so a fresh `git clone` on a Windows
# machine would produce a repository whose installers cannot run, while every file looks
# correct in an editor. The README's clone-then-install path depends on this file.
#
# eol=lf pins the WORKING COPY, not just the stored blob, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.mdc  text eol=lf
*.tsv  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
